                <pb facs="0425" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg345"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Wilson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay acknowledges receipt of Mr. Buck’s dispatch No. 532, and directs Mr.
                    Wilson to request the Japanese Government to withhold its decision until the
                    Department can have time to prepare and forward its views on questions of
                    property leases, their registration, etc.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
